Xtrata (XST)

Deterministic Participation Token Whitepaper

Version 1.0 – Emissions + Claims Specification

⸻

1. Overview

XST is the native participation token of the Xtrata protocol.

XST is not sold, not pre-mined, and not governed after deployment.
It is emitted deterministically over a fixed period and distributed to participants based on on-chain history.

The purpose of XST is to:
	•	encode early participation,
	•	reward long-term engagement,
	•	and act as a permanent economic fossil record of Xtrata’s growth.

Once emissions end, XST becomes a fixed-supply historical asset.

⸻

2. Core Principles
	1.	Fixed Supply
Total XST supply is capped at 1,000,000,000 tokens.
	2.	Deterministic Emissions
Emissions follow a fixed, block-based schedule.
No admin controls, no future minting.
	3.	Delayed Start
Emissions do not begin until inscription #1000 is minted.
	4.	Inscription-Centric Rewards
Token earnings are primarily tied to inscription ownership.
Early inscription IDs permanently earn slightly more.
	5.	Claim-Based Distribution
Tokens are claimed by users.
The contract never loops over participants or pushes payouts.

⸻

3. Token Supply and Timeline

3.1 Total Supply

TOTAL_SUPPLY = 1,000,000,000 XST

3.2 Emission Start
	•	Emissions begin only once inscription ID 1000 exists
	•	At that moment:

emissionsStartBlock = current block height



3.3 Emission Duration
	•	Emissions run for exactly 4 years worth of blocks

Assuming ~10 minute blocks:

BLOCKS_PER_YEAR ≈ 52,560
DURATION_BLOCKS ≈ 210,240

After:

emissionsStartBlock + DURATION_BLOCKS

→ emissions are permanently zero.

⸻

4. Emission Schedule (Per Block)

XST emissions are block-based, not event-based.

4.1 Yearly Front-Loaded Schedule (Familiar Model)

Year	Share	Tokens
Year 1	40%	400,000,000
Year 2	30%	300,000,000
Year 3	20%	200,000,000
Year 4	10%	100,000,000

Each year has a fixed per-block rate:

perBlockRate = yearAllocation / blocksInThatYear

4.2 Hard Cap Enforcement

The contract tracks:

totalEmitted

On every update:

newEmission = min(remainingSupply, blocksElapsed × perBlockRate)

This guarantees:
	•	emissions never exceed 1B
	•	emissions always end on time
	•	any rounding remainder is paid out in the final blocks

⸻

5. Distribution Model (Simple + Safe)

Chosen Model: Global Accumulator (Simplest Claims)

This is the same pattern used by proven staking systems.

Key idea
	•	The protocol maintains a global “reward per weight” accumulator.
	•	Each inscription claims based on how much the accumulator has grown since its last claim.

No iteration. No snapshots. No admin logic.

⸻

6. Inscription Weighting (Option A – Gentle Early Advantage)

Each inscription has a fixed weight, determined only by its tokenId.

6.1 Weight Bands

Inscription IDs	Weight
0	1400
1–10	1200
11–100	1000
101–1,000	800
1,001–10,000	640
10,001–100,000	512
100,001–1,000,000	410
…	×4/5 per decade

Formula for bands ≥ 101:

nextWeight = floor(previousWeight × 4 / 5)

This produces:
	•	a gentle drop from 0 → 100
	•	permanent rarity value for early IDs
	•	diminishing advantage at scale
	•	integer-only math

⸻

7. Owner Pool Allocation

Each block’s emission is split as follows:

OWNER_POOL = 70%
(optional) PARTICIPANT_POOL = 30%

This whitepaper defines OWNER_POOL only, for maximal simplicity.

(Participant pool can be added later without affecting determinism.)

⸻

8. Accumulator Mechanics (Exact Claim Logic)

8.1 Global State Variables

accRewardPerWeight   // scaled integer
lastEmissionBlock
totalWeightMinted

8.2 On Inscription Mint

When a new inscription is created:

weight = weightForTokenId(tokenId)
totalWeightMinted += weight
store inscriptionWeight[tokenId] = weight
store inscriptionRewardDebt[tokenId] = accRewardPerWeight


⸻

8.3 Updating Emissions (Lazy)

Whenever any claim happens:
	1.	Calculate elapsed blocks since last update
	2.	Calculate how many tokens should have been emitted
	3.	Increase accumulator:

accRewardPerWeight += (newEmission × OWNER_POOL) / totalWeightMinted
lastEmissionBlock = currentBlock
totalEmitted += newEmission

No looping. O(1).

⸻

8.4 Claiming Rewards

When the owner of inscription tokenId calls claim(tokenId):

pending =
  inscriptionWeight[tokenId] ×
  (accRewardPerWeight - inscriptionRewardDebt[tokenId])

Then:

transfer pending XST to current owner
inscriptionRewardDebt[tokenId] = accRewardPerWeight

That’s it.

